# Myriad (CR 702.116a): in a four-player game Wyrm's Crossing Patrol attacks Bot2, so Bot1 is asked in turn order about each of the other two
# opponents, Bot3 then Bot4, and creates a token for each (they enter together, CR 614.1c): one attacking Bot3, one attacking Bot4.
# Each opponent takes 1, and so does Bot2; the tokens are exiled at end of combat. Mox Pearl pays for the Patrol.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Wyrm's Crossing Patrol
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot4 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot4.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot4.Pass
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot3)
Bot1.Target(Bot4)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot4.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2; Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot3; Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot4
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Bot3.Life = 19
? Bot4.Life = 19

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
Exile.Count = 0
